1. e4 c5 2. Nf3 d6 3. d4 cxd4 4. Nxd4 Nf6 5. Nc3 a6 6. Be3 Ng4
7. Bg5 { The bishop escapes the knight's attack and eyes the e7 pawn, so Black cannot ignore it. }
7... h6
(7... Nc6 8. Bh4)
8. Bh4 { Keeps the bishop on the board, away from the pawns that want to hit it. } 8... g5
(8... Nc6 9. Be2)
9. Bg3 { Keeps the bishop on the board. On g3 it still eyes the d6 pawn. }
9... Bg7
10. h3 { Kicks the knight, so Black must decide where it goes. }
10... Ne5
11. Nf5 { Puts the knight on an active square where it eyes the bishop on g7 and the d6 pawn. Black usually trades it off. [%csl Gf5] }
11... Bxf5
12. exf5 *
